{
  "_comment": "The canonical wire (RFC 8785) of a snapshot's context: object keys sorted by UTF-16 code unit, numbers as ECMAScript Number::toString writes them, strings as JSON.stringify escapes them. Each case's context is parsed and serialized inside the envelope {\"machine\":\"m\",\"version\":1,\"state\":\"S\",\"context\":...}; 'wire' is the context part of the result. A context that a JSON parser cannot carry is given as UTF-16 code units instead: 'stringUnits' is the context {\"s\":<the string>}, 'keyUnits' the context {<the string>:1}. Every engine reads this file; add a vector here, not in one engine's tests.",
